@startuml
title AI Assistance Design Sequence Diagram

actor "Primary User" as User
participant "React Web Client" as Client
participant "Laravel REST API" as API
participant "AI Assistance Module" as Assistance
participant "Authorization Service" as Authorization
participant "Context Minimizer" as Minimizer
database "Communication Store" as Store
participant "Selected AI Provider" as AIProvider

User -> Client : request summary or reply suggestion
Client -> API : submit AI assistance request
API -> Authorization : verify user ownership
Authorization -> Store : check conversation ownership
Store --> Authorization : ownership result

alt access permitted
  Authorization --> API : access granted
  API -> Assistance : create AI assistance request
  Assistance -> Store : retrieve selected conversation
  Store --> Assistance : conversation data
  Assistance -> Minimizer : minimize required context
  Minimizer --> Assistance : approved request context
  Assistance -> AIProvider : submit minimized context

  alt AI request succeeds
    AIProvider --> Assistance : summary or reply suggestion
    Assistance --> API : generated result
    API --> Client : display result for review
    Client --> User : show editable AI result
    User -> Client : edit, accept, or discard result
    Client -> API : save user decision
    API --> Client : decision recorded
  else AI request fails
    AIProvider --> Assistance : failure response
    Assistance --> API : AI unavailable status
    API --> Client : display failure
    Client --> User : show failure without blocking core features
  end
else access denied
  Authorization --> API : access denied
  API --> Client : forbidden response
  Client --> User : display access error
end

note over Assistance,AIProvider
AI output is assistive and untrusted.
AI must never send content autonomously.
end note

note over User,API
Any external sending requires a separate product decision
and explicit user approval.
end note

@enduml
